{"content_hash": "f6a927d63377904d", "version_id": 634, "article_id": 64, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Sudan border strikes kill 72 gold miners, rights group says", "title_zh": "苏丹边境空袭致72名淘金者死亡，人权组织称", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqy43vrk8wv8o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1621837593522-eae4fc6a9f17?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8N3x8ZG96ZW5zJTIwZ29sZCUyMHByb3NwZWN0b3JzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE3NjYxMzJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Kanchanara on Unsplash", "author": "Kanchanara", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@kanchanara?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/silver-and-black-round-pendant-necklace-tayj2w_LCHI?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(69, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(107, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "8fb5b734dbc5"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 229, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "A regional rights group says at least 72 civilians were killed in air strikes on gold mining sites in Sudan. Neither Egypt nor Sudan's de facto authorities have commented on the attack.", "lead_zh": "一个地区人权组织称，苏丹金矿场遭空袭，至少72名平民死亡。埃及和苏丹实际掌权当局均未就此作出回应。", "preview": "At least 72 civilians who were prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, according to a regional rig", "preview_zh": "据一个地区人权组织称，苏丹边境地区至少72名淘金平民在空袭中丧生。总部位于喀土穆的“紧急律师”组织表示，周六战机袭击了尼罗河州热门金矿场的矿工。埃及政府和苏丹实际掌权当局迄今均未置评。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 622, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/64/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 90.025, "size_bytes": 543888, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 252, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0c12f88/content/data/versions/634.json", "paragraphs": ["At least 72 civilians who were prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, according to a regional rights group. Emergency Lawyers, based in Khartoum, said jets targeted the miners at popular gold mining sites in River Nile state on Saturday. Neither the Egyptian government nor Sudan's de facto authorities have commented so far.", "Cairo has previously faced accusations of deadly strikes on gold prospectors as part of a crackdown on illegal activity along its southern border. Emergency Lawyers said these earlier attacks violated Sudan's sovereign territory and showed the government's lack of control over the region. In a statement on Sunday, the group said the deliberate targeting of unarmed civilians may constitute war crimes.", "The Paris-based Sudan Tribune reported that the death toll could be much higher, citing a survivor who said many more people were injured. Eyewitnesses said the attack began around 06:00 local time, with aircraft firing more than five missiles at the miners' camps, destroying them and excavation pits with people still inside.", "Gold lies at the core of the border tensions. Sudan's civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining, which is often risky and done without official permission. Egypt's border force said in June it had seized 86 tonnes of gold ore and amateur prospecting equipment. Smuggled gold may also fund armed insurgent groups."], "paragraphs_zh": ["据一个地区人权组织称，苏丹边境地区至少72名淘金平民在空袭中丧生。总部位于喀土穆的“紧急律师”组织表示，周六战机袭击了尼罗河州热门金矿场的矿工。埃及政府和苏丹实际掌权当局迄今均未置评。", "开罗此前曾被指控在打击南部边境非法活动的行动中对淘金者发动致命袭击。“紧急律师”组织称，这些早前的袭击侵犯了苏丹主权领土，表明政府对该地区缺乏控制。该组织在周日声明中表示，故意针对手无寸铁的平民可能构成战争罪。", "总部位于巴黎的《苏丹论坛报》援引一名幸存者的话报道称，死亡人数可能远高于此，许多人受伤。目击者称，袭击于当地时间约6点开始，飞机向矿工营地发射了五枚以上导弹，摧毁了营地和仍有人的挖掘坑。", "黄金是边境紧张局势的核心。苏丹内战导致手工采矿激增，这种采矿往往风险高且未经官方许可。埃及边防部队6月表示，已查获86吨金矿石和业余勘探设备。走私黄金也可能为武装叛乱组织提供资金。"], "body": "At least 72 civilians who were prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, according to a regional rights group. Emergency Lawyers, based in Khartoum, said jets targeted the miners at popular gold mining sites in River Nile state on Saturday. Neither the Egyptian government nor Sudan's de facto authorities have commented so far.\n\nCairo has previously faced accusations of deadly strikes on gold prospectors as part of a crackdown on illegal activity along its southern border. Emergency Lawyers said these earlier attacks violated Sudan's sovereign territory and showed the government's lack of control over the region. In a statement on Sunday, the group said the deliberate targeting of unarmed civilians may constitute war crimes.\n\nThe Paris-based Sudan Tribune reported that the death toll could be much higher, citing a survivor who said many more people were injured. Eyewitnesses said the attack began around 06:00 local time, with aircraft firing more than five missiles at the miners' camps, destroying them and excavation pits with people still inside.\n\nGold lies at the core of the border tensions. Sudan's civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining, which is often risky and done without official permission. Egypt's border force said in June it had seized 86 tonnes of gold ore and amateur prospecting equipment. Smuggled gold may also fund armed insurgent groups.", "body_zh": "据一个地区人权组织称，苏丹边境地区至少72名淘金平民在空袭中丧生。总部位于喀土穆的“紧急律师”组织表示，周六战机袭击了尼罗河州热门金矿场的矿工。埃及政府和苏丹实际掌权当局迄今均未置评。\n\n开罗此前曾被指控在打击南部边境非法活动的行动中对淘金者发动致命袭击。“紧急律师”组织称，这些早前的袭击侵犯了苏丹主权领土，表明政府对该地区缺乏控制。该组织在周日声明中表示，故意针对手无寸铁的平民可能构成战争罪。\n\n总部位于巴黎的《苏丹论坛报》援引一名幸存者的话报道称，死亡人数可能远高于此，许多人受伤。目击者称，袭击于当地时间约6点开始，飞机向矿工营地发射了五枚以上导弹，摧毁了营地和仍有人的挖掘坑。\n\n黄金是边境紧张局势的核心。苏丹内战导致手工采矿激增，这种采矿往往风险高且未经官方许可。埃及边防部队6月表示，已查获86吨金矿石和业余勘探设备。走私黄金也可能为武装叛乱组织提供资金。", "text": "At least 72 civilians who were prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, according to a regional rights group. Emergency Lawyers, based in Khartoum, said jets targeted the miners at popular gold mining sites in River Nile state on Saturday. Neither the Egyptian government nor Sudan's de facto authorities have commented so far. Cairo has previously faced accusations of deadly strikes on gold prospectors as part of a crackdown on illegal activity along its southern border. Emergency Lawyers said these earlier attacks violated Sudan's sovereign territory and showed the government's lack of control over the region. In a statement on Sunday, the group said the deliberate targeting of unarmed civilians may constitute war crimes. The Paris-based Sudan Tribune reported that the death toll could be much higher, citing a survivor who said many more people were injured. Eyewitnesses said the attack began around 06:00 local time, with aircraft firing more than five missiles at the miners' camps, destroying them and excavation pits with people still inside. Gold lies at the core of the border tensions. Sudan's civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining, which is often risky and done without official permission. Egypt's border force said in June it had seized 86 tonnes of gold ore and amateur prospecting equipment. Smuggled gold may also fund armed insurgent groups.", "vocab": [{"word": "prospector", "pos": "noun", "zh": "勘探者，淘金者", "note": "指寻找金矿等资源的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "air strike", "pos": "noun", "zh": "空袭", "note": "常与 carry out, launch 搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "civilian", "pos": "noun", "zh": "平民", "note": "与军人相对", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "de facto", "pos": "adj", "zh": "实际上的", "note": "指虽无合法名义但实际掌权", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "crackdown", "pos": "noun", "zh": "镇压，打击", "note": "常与 on 连用，如 crackdown on crime", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "sovereign", "pos": "adj", "zh": "主权的", "note": "sovereign territory 主权领土", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "deliberate", "pos": "adj", "zh": "故意的，蓄意的", "note": "deliberate targeting 故意针对", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "humanitarian", "pos": "adj", "zh": "人道主义的", "note": "international humanitarian law 国际人道法", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "provisional", "pos": "adj", "zh": "临时的，暂定的", "note": "provisional death toll 暂定死亡人数", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "artisanal", "pos": "adj", "zh": "手工的", "note": "artisanal mining 手工采矿", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "smuggle", "pos": "verb", "zh": "走私", "note": "smuggled gold 走私黄金", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "insurgent", "pos": "noun", "zh": "叛乱分子", "note": "armed insurgent groups 武装叛乱组织", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says", "summary_original": "Neither Egypt nor Sudan has commented on the alleged strikes on an artisanal mining camp on Saturday.", "body_original": "Dozens of gold prospectors killed in strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says\nBy\nAleks Phillips\nPublished\n3 hours ago\nAt least 72 civilians who had been prospecting for gold in a border region of Sudan have been killed in air strikes, a regional rights group says.\nEmergency Lawyers, based in the Sudanese capital, Khartoum, said jets targeted the so-called artisanal miners at a popular gold mining sites in Sudan's River Nile state on Saturday.\nNeither the Egyptian government nor the de facto Sudanese authorities have so far commented.\nCairo has previously faced accusations of deadly strikes on gold prospectors as part of a crackdown on illicit activity along its southern border.\nEmergency Lawyers noted the previous alleged attacks and said they represented not only a violation of Sudan's sovereign territory but demonstrated the government's lack of control over the region.\n\"The deliberate targeting of unarmed civilians violates international humanitarian law and the right to life,\" it said in a statement on Sunday. \"These acts may constitute war crimes.\"\nIt noted that its death toll was provisional and could rise.\nThe Paris-based Sudan Tribune reported that the death toll could far exceed the number reported by Emergency Lawyers, citing a survivor of Saturday's attack who said many more people had been injured.\nEyewitnesses said the attack began around 06:00 local time (04:00 GMT), with the aircraft firing more than five missiles directly at the miners' camps, destroying them and excavation pits with people still inside, the newspaper wrote.\nThe Sudan Tribune reported claims in June that Egyptian forces had used drones and artillery to target artisanal mining sites in the same region, killing several, after sporadic incidents of Egyptian border guards of burning equipment, torching temporary shelters, and firing live ammunition to disperse mine workers.\nDays later, Egypt's border agency announced that it and the military had begun a sweeping security campaign along the border to foil illegal migration, drug smuggling and illegal mining.\nAt the same time, Sudan's de facto leader announced an investigation into the alleged strikes, which were said to have killed dozens.\nGold lies at the core of the border tensions.\nSudan's ongoing civil war has led to a surge in artisanal mining - an often risky practice conducted by civilians with rudimentary tools and without official permission - particularly in remote areas near its borders.\nGold-rich areas such as those in River Nile state lie along porous borders in terrain historically associated with cross-border smuggling routes, with artisanally mined gold potentially feeding into those channels.\nEgypt's border force said in June that it had seized 86 tonnes of gold ore along with amateur prospecting equipment.\nArtisanal mining has also reportedly continued in Sudan's conflict zones and smuggled gold may be a source of income for armed insurgent groups.\nThis has raised concerns of illicit Sudanese gold undermining the legitimate Egyptian gold market.\nRelated topics\nSudan\nEgypt\nAfrica\nMining\nMore on this story\nA simple guide to what is happening in Sudan\nPublished\n13 November 2025", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:48:50.607058", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "At", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.312, "sm": 100, "em": 312, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "least", "s": 0.325, "e": 0.588, "sm": 325, "em": 587, "cs": 3, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "72", "s": 0.6, "e": 1.288, "sm": 600, "em": 1287, "cs": 9, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "civilians", "s": 1.3, "e": 1.95, "sm": 1300, "em": 1950, "cs": 12, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "who", "s": 1.962, "e": 2.05, "sm": 1962, "em": 2050, "cs": 22, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "were", "s": 2.062, "e": 2.188, "sm": 2062, "em": 2187, "cs": 26, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "prospecting", "s": 2.2, "e": 2.9, "sm": 2200, "em": 2900, "cs": 31, "ce": 42, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "for", "s": 2.913, "e": 3.062, "sm": 2912, "em": 3062, "cs": 43, "ce": 46, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "gold", "s": 3.075, "e": 3.413, "sm": 3075, "em": 3412, "cs": 47, "ce": 51, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "in", "s": 3.425, "e": 3.525, "sm": 3425, "em": 3525, "cs": 52, "ce": 54, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "a", "s": 3.538, "e": 3.6, "sm": 3537, "em": 3600, "cs": 55, "ce": 56, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "border", "s": 3.612, "e": 3.987, "sm": 3612, "em": 3987, "cs": 57, "ce": 63, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "region", "s": 4.0, "e": 4.312, "sm": 4000, "em": 4312, "cs": 64, "ce": 70, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "of", "s": 4.325, "e": 4.4, "sm": 4325, "em": 4400, "cs": 71, "ce": 73, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "Sudan", "s": 4.412, "e": 4.912, "sm": 4412, "em": 4912, "cs": 74, "ce": 79, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "have", "s": 4.925, "e": 5.087, "sm": 4925, "em": 5087, "cs": 80, "ce": 84, "si": 0}, {"i": 16, "w": "been", "s": 5.1, "e": 5.262, "sm": 5100, "em": 5262, "cs": 85, "ce": 89, "si": 0}, {"i": 17, "w": "killed", "s": 5.275, "e": 5.613, "sm": 5275, "em": 5612, "cs": 90, "ce": 96, "si": 0}, {"i": 18, "w": "in", "s": 5.625, "e": 5.75, "sm": 5625, "em": 5